# CE-QUAL-W2 — Tijuana River Estuary (TJRE) Model

CE-QUAL-W2 (Corps of Engineers Width-Averaged 2-D model) is used in this repo to simulate hydrodynamic and water quality behavior in the Tijuana River Estuary, as part of this thesis project.

## Version & Platform

- This repo is built for **CE-QUAL-W2 v4.5**. Files here (executables, examples, manual) are pinned to that version and may not match other versions available on the official CE-QUAL-W2 site.
- **CE-QUAL-W2's executables are Windows-only.** They will not run natively on macOS.
- **File Maker executable:** earlier CE-QUAL-W2 versions required a separate File Maker executable to convert raw output text files (`.npt`/`.opt`) into `.csv` for analysis. **v4.5 no longer requires this step** — output files can be read directly.

## Repo Structure

| Folder | Contents |
|---|---|
| `Executables/` | `prew2.exe` (preprocessor), `w2.exe` (model), `w2post.exe` (post-processor / output viewer) — v4.5 only |
| `Examples/` | Official CE-QUAL-W2 example model files |
| `Manual/` | Official CE-QUAL-W2 v4.5 user manual |
| `TJRE_runs/` | One folder per model run, each with input files, a spreadsheet of all runs' parameters, and a results/stats spreadsheet |
| `Model_Analysis/` | R scripts for QA/QC and plotting model output against field observations |

The Esecutables, Examples, and Manual are also available from the official CE-QUAL-W2 website; they're bundled here to pin the exact v4.5 versions used for this thesis and save you the download.

## How to Run a Model

1. Download the run folder you want from `TJRE_runs/`.
2. Download `Model_Analysis/` — you'll need it to check results later.
3. Download `Executables/`. (If you'd rather not grab the whole folder, you need at least `prew2.exe` and `w2.exe` to run the model, and `w2post.exe` separately to view results afterward.)
4. Unzip everything into the same working directory as the run's input files.
Optional Steps (needed if you want to make changes to the model): 
- Open the w2_con_allbranches.xlsx file.
- Make any changes, save the file, then click the export to csv button (make sure that Excel macros are enabled). 
5. Run `prew2.exe` (the preprocessor) first.
   - **Known issue:** v4.5's preprocessor has a bug (an off-by-one error in `pre_ivf_45.f90`, ~line 3794) that can throw an error. If `prew2.exe` errors out, skip it — run `w2_v4_64.exe` directly instead. The model runs correctly without the preprocessor step in that case.
6. If `prew2.exe` completes without error, run `w2.exe` next.
7. Watch the loading bar at the bottom of the console window to track progress.

## Viewing Model Results

1. Run `w2post.exe` from `Executables/`.
2. When prompted, click **Browse** and select the folder where your model output was generated (wherever you ran `w2.exe` / `w2_v4_64.exe`).
3. For the R scripts in `Model_Analysis/`, update the file paths at the top of each script to point to your local output folder.
   - The scripts primarily read the `.tsr` (time series) and `.spr` (profile) output files.

## Reference

The official CE-QUAL-W2 manual and examples are also available at the [CE-QUAL-W2 site](https://www.ce-qual-w2.org) if you need documentation beyond what's bundled in `Manual/`.                                                                                            
                                                                                                


